🚽 curve.brainrot — the difficulty curve.
🚽
🚽 One variable, `speed`, drives scrolling, spawn spacing, the HUD level and
🚽 the sky. Nothing in the simulation branches on the *level* except the sky
🚽 palette, which is a cosmetic decision that wants to be steppy.
🚽
🚽 Every function here is pure and scalar-only, which is what makes the
🚽 curve testable without opening a window. See DESIGN.md sections 7 and 8.

🚽 Continuous speed, quantised into the eight segments the HUD draws.
🚽 Returns 1 .. 8.
rizz speed_to_lvl(chad speed) {
    rizz lvl = 1 + (speed - t_speed_start()) / 90.0;
    edgy (lvl < 1) { bussin 1; }
    edgy (lvl > 8) { bussin 8; }
    bussin lvl;
}

🚽 Seconds between spawns, before jitter and before the fairness clamp.
🚽
🚽 Spacing is measured in TIME, never in pixels. A pixel gap that is
🚽 generous at 260 px/s is lethal at 900 px/s; a time gap stays reactable
🚽 as the world accelerates. This is the difference between hard and
🚽 unfair, and it is the most important rule in the game.
chad spawn_gap(chad speed) {
    chad gap = t_gap_base() - speed * t_gap_slope();
    bussin maxf(gap, t_gap_min());
}

🚽 True when a kind has to be jumped rather than bonked.
cap kind_is_jump(rizz kind) {
    edgy (kind == t_kind_patapim()) { bussin L; }
    bussin W;
}

🚽 The fairness clamp, applied after jitter.
🚽
🚽 Two consecutive jump-required spawns need at least one full jump arc
🚽 (0.77s at the shipped gravity) plus a reaction buffer -- you have to be
🚽 able to land before the next one arrives. Everything else gets the
🚽 absolute floor.
🚽
🚽 Any spawn the player cannot avoid is a bug, not a difficulty setting.
chad fair_clamp(chad gap, rizz prev_kind, rizz kind) {
    cap a = kind_is_jump(prev_kind);
    cap b = kind_is_jump(kind);
    edgy (a) {
        edgy (b) {
            bussin maxf(gap, t_fair_jump_jump());
        }
    }
    bussin maxf(gap, t_fair_any());
}

🚽 Which kind to spawn next, from a PRNG draw and the current level.
🚽
🚽 Patapim shows up just under half the time. The tall post only appears
🚽 from level 2, so the first few seconds teach the crate jump cleanly.
rizz pick_kind(rizz draw, rizz lvl) {
    rizz r = draw % 100;
    edgy (r < 45) { bussin t_kind_patapim(); }
    edgy (lvl < 2) { bussin t_kind_crate(); }
    edgy (r < 75) { bussin t_kind_crate(); }
    bussin t_kind_post();
}

chad kind_w(rizz kind) {
    edgy (kind == t_kind_crate())   { bussin 48.0; }
    edgy (kind == t_kind_post())    { bussin 40.0; }
    bussin 64.0;
}

chad kind_h(rizz kind) {
    edgy (kind == t_kind_crate())   { bussin 48.0; }
    edgy (kind == t_kind_post())    { bussin 96.0; }
    bussin 64.0;
}

🚽 --- sky palette, 03:30 -> 05:00 ---
🚽 Discrete per level tier. A smooth lerp needs no new API and can replace
🚽 this later; steps are chosen because they make the player notice they
🚽 survived another tier.
rizz sky_r(rizz lvl) {
    edgy (lvl <= 2) { bussin 12; }
    edgy (lvl <= 4) { bussin 18; }
    edgy (lvl <= 6) { bussin 38; }
    edgy (lvl <= 7) { bussin 78; }
    bussin 140;
}

rizz sky_g(rizz lvl) {
    edgy (lvl <= 2) { bussin 14; }
    edgy (lvl <= 4) { bussin 20; }
    edgy (lvl <= 6) { bussin 30; }
    edgy (lvl <= 7) { bussin 44; }
    bussin 74;
}

rizz sky_b(rizz lvl) {
    edgy (lvl <= 2) { bussin 34; }
    edgy (lvl <= 4) { bussin 48; }
    edgy (lvl <= 6) { bussin 64; }
    edgy (lvl <= 7) { bussin 66; }
    bussin 60;
}
